%N A398215 Decimal expansion of the long/short edge length ratio of a canonical (dual-uniform) octagonal trapezohedron.
%C A398215 The octagonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the octagonal antiprism.
%H A398215 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398215/b398215.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398215 David I. McCooey, <a href="https://dmccooey.com/polyhedra/OctagonalTrapezohedron.html">Octagonal Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398215 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Octagonal_antitegum">Octagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398215 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398215 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_04">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 4</a>.
%F A398215 Equals (csc(Pi/16)^2)/4.
%F A398215 Equals the largest root of 2*x^4 - 16*x^3 + 20*x^2 - 8*x + 1.
%e A398215 6.5685355922720450889146982764304618057982663154535...
%t A398215 First[RealDigits[Csc[Pi/16]^2/4, 10, 100]]
%t A398215 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398215 First[RealDigits[Max[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 8}, "EdgeLengths"]], 10, 100]]
